{"id":442806395,"author":{"login":"sooperset","id":32061883,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDYxODgz","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDONYN7OM4aZLB7","tag_name":"v0.24.3","target_commitish":"caebfa0f01719ad1e0a32265d70449a94c847776","name":"v0.24.3","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-12T10:43:12Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T10:43:25Z","published_at":"2026-11-12T10:43:25Z","assets":[],"body":"## 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n- **Windows: attachments and file inputs work again.** Since 0.24.1, every file read or write through the confined file opener failed on Windows with `PermissionError: [Errno 13]`. This broke Jira attachment upload and download by path, Confluence attachments, and `content_file`. Windows now opens the file by path with the same boundary and symlink checks. Linux and macOS keep the directory-anchored open (#1832, #1835). Thanks to @Fabbul for the report and @PerryLink for the fix.\n- **Tests: macOS.** `test_stdio_keeps_wide_cwd` no longer fails on macOS, where `/etc` is a symlink (#1830). Thanks to @mhollingsworth-cs.\n","mentions_count":3}
